					<h1 class="title" title="Places to see in Ludhiana">Places to see in Ludhiana</h1>
					<div class="entry-content">
<h3>Location:</h3>
<p>Today <b>Ludhiana</b> is <b>densely populated cities of India</b> situated in the state of <b>Punjab</b>. 
It got its name from the <b>Lodhi dynasty</b> in 1480. The <b>river Sutlej</b> separates Ludhiana from the 
city of <b>Jalandhar</b>. Ludhiana is world famous for its textile and light engineering industries. The 
famous university, <b>Punjab agricultural university</b> is also located on the <b>outskirts of Ludhiana</b>. 
It organizes the <b>Kisaan Mela</b> every year.  Ludhiana is also an <b>important pilgrimage centre</b> of the 
Sikhs as there are many <b>Gurudwaras</b> in and around the city.</p>

<h3>Places to see:</h3>
<p>There are many places sightseeing and <b>tourist attractions in Ludhiana</b>. The <b>fort of Lodhi</b>, 
built by Sikander Lodhi some 500 years ago is situated on the banks of river Sutlej. It is a <b>famous 
historical monument</b>. About 10km. from Ludhiana is situated the famous <b>Gurudwara Shrimanji Sahib Alamgir</b>. This place is 
significant because it was here that the <b>pacifist Sikh clan</b> was converted to a martial community by 
the last Sikh guru, <b>Guru Gobind Singh</b>. The <b>‘Khalsa’</b> was introduced here by him. Every year in 
December, a fair is held. Another place of interest is the <b>Phillaur fort</b> which is now a place of 
police training center. Designed by <b>Dewan Mohkam Chand</b>, it is a historical fort of ancient times. </p>


<p><b>Pir-I-Dastgir</b> shrine is a famous shrine of Peer Abdul Kadar Gilani that draws both Hindu and 
<b>Muslim devotees</b> towards it. It is located in the <b>north-west part of Ludhiana</b>. Some of the some 
other places of religious importance are <b>Gurudwara Charan Kamal , Gurudwara Nanaksar Jagraon,</b> the 
<b>famous tombs of Hussain Khan</b> and <b>Bahadur Khan</b> and  the <b>Bilwanwali Masjid</b>.  A place of 
popular tourist attraction is the <b>Nehru Rose Garden</b> spread over an area of 30 acres in the posh area 
of Ludhiana. About 17,000 plants and 16, 00 varieties of roses and numerous fountains make this place a 
centre of relaxation. A <b>rose festival</b> is held here every year. Located on the GT Road, 6 km. from the main 
city, is a fantabulous <b>tiger safari</b> known as the <b>Tiger Zoo</b>. Varieties of majestic tigers can be seen here.</p> 

<p>A lovely amusement park, the main attraction not only for the kids but all age groups is the amazing 
<b>Harry’s World</b>. The main attractions are ice –skating and snowfall. It boasts to be the <b>third biggest 
indoor snow world</b>. The rural museum and the war museum are other places of tourist visit. Ludhiana, 
also known as <b>‘Lancaster of India’</b> has become quite famous as a <b>tourist attraction city</b>. </p>





